  "dct_description_sm": [
    "# Afghanistan Earthquake: Damage Proxy Maps, Oct 2023 The **Earth Observatory of Singapore – Remote Sensing Lab (EOS-RS)** produced these damage proxy maps for Afghanistan Earthquake (Oct 2023) from synthetic aperture radar (SAR) satellite images. Each map is a separate ZIP below with its GeoTIFF, a KMZ for Google Earth, the PNG figures and a text file describing how it was made and how to read it. ## Maps in this dataset - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Afghanistan, Earthquake, 13 Oct 2023, v0.5 ** - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Afghanistan, Earthquake, 13 Oct 2023, v0.5 ** - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Afghanistan, Earthquake, 8 Oct 2023, v1.2** - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Afghanistan, Earthquake, 8 Oct 2023, v1.2** - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Afghanistan, Earthquake, 8 Oct 2023, v0.9** (superseded) - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Afghanistan, Earthquake, 8 Oct 2023, v0.5** (superseded) - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Afghanistan, Earthquake, 8 Oct 2023, v0.5** (superseded) - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Afghanistan, Earthquake, 7 Oct 2023, v0.9** - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Afghanistan, Earthquake, 7 Oct 2023, v0.5** - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Afghanistan, Earthquake, 7 Oct 2023, v0.5** (superseded) **More map details and files:** **More map details and files:** **Credits:** Earth Observatory of Singapore - Remote Sensing Lab (EOS-RS), Original data ALOS-2 PALSAR-2 Product - JAXA (2022)"
